.TH TPAD 1 "17 July 2026" "" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
tpad \- GTK based simple, fast, and easy to use text editor.

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tpad
.RI [ FILE ... ]
.br

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBtpad\fP is a GTK text editor for plain text and source files.
.PP
Use \fBFile \(-> Print...\fP or press \fBCtrl+P\fP to open the system GTK
print dialog. The dialog provides the printers, print-to-file destination,
paper size, orientation, page range, and other options supplied by the
desktop print service.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Ctrl+P
Open the system print dialog for the current document.
.TP
.B Ctrl+,
Open the Preferences window.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit tpad.
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Reverse the current text.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Z
Redo the most recently undone edit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.tpad.cfg
Per-user configuration data.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lp (1)
